{"version": 2, "width": 110, "height": 24, "timestamp": 1795524700, "title": "design/pricing-page \u00b7 ambitious run 5", "env": {"TERM": "xterm-256color"}, "theme": {"fg": "#d8dee9", "bg": "#1e1f1c", "palette": "#272822:#f92672:#a6e22e:#f4bf75:#66d9ef:#ae81ff:#a1efe4:#f8f8f2:#75715e:#f92672:#a6e22e:#f4bf75:#66d9ef:#ae81ff:#a1efe4:#f9f8f5"}}
[0.0, "o", "\u001b[?25l"]
[0.0, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Design a pricing page for an invoicing app for freelancers, as a single web page\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[34.504, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mWrote 1 file\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Write(<workspace>/pricing.html)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[39.587, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I built the pricing page as a single self-contained file at `<workspace>/pricing.html`. I haven't opened it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  in a browser, so the layout and the billing toggle are untested.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Plans**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Starter, $0:** 3 clients and 5 invoices a month.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Freelancer, $12/mo billed yearly or $15 monthly:** this is the highlighted \"Most popular\" plan. It has\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  unlimited invoices, branding, automatic reminders, recurring invoices and time tracking.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Studio, $28/mo billed yearly or $35 monthly:** it adds 5 team members, multi-currency, accounting sync\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and priority support.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The product name (Inkwell), prices, limits, testimonial and discount are all placeholders I made up. Swap in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  your real ones.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Page sections, top to bottom**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - A headline and a Monthly/Yearly toggle with a \"Save 20%\" badge. The toggle changes the prices and the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  billing note.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The three plan cards.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - A note that payment processing fees aren't marked up.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - A comparison table that scrolls sideways on small screens.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - A testimonial.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - An FAQ covering cancelling, plan limits, fees, discounts and data export.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - A closing call to action.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Design**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - It uses a warm off-white background, a deep green accent and serif headings, so it looks less like a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  generic SaaS page.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - It switches to dark mode automatically.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The cards stack into one column on mobile.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - It includes focus outlines, ARIA labels on the toggle and reduced-motion support.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - It needs no build step and no external assets. The only JavaScript is the small toggle script.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  If you'd like a different brand name or color palette, or a version in React or Tailwind, tell me and I'll\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  change it.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[39.886, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m⚑ Stop hook: Before you finish, unless the task was trivial (a typo, a rename, a one-line answer), end with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m  one question, using AskUserQuestion when it's available:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ⎿  … +5 lines of instructions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[43.16, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I could push the page further in three ways:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **Check it in a browser.** I'd screenshot desktop, mobile and dark mode, then fix any layout problems.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Add interactivity.** This would be a \"how many invoices do you send?\" slider that recommends a plan,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and an annual-savings figure on each card.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **Add a brand and trust pass.** I'd add a simple logo mark, a row of client or integration logos, and a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  money-back guarantee line.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Each step is small. I'd expect the whole thing to cost less than building the page did.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Do you want me to push on **step by step** (you see each result before the next) or **straight through**? Or\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  we can stop here.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[47.919, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[97m❯ Push it further.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
