[351.344, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ The page is rebuilt around one idea: it reads as an invoice, with the brand name Inkwell still in place.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I've checked the fixed render and the automated checks. I haven't compared v1 and v2 side by side at full\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  length, and I haven't run the cold 5-second test on someone else.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What changed**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Look:** cream paper, navy ink and one stamp-red accent. Headings are in a classic serif and the metadata\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  is in a monospace. The hero opens with an invoice header (\"Invoice № 0001 · Bill to: You, freelancer ·\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Terms: Cancel anytime\") above the headline \"Get paid like the *pro* you are.\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Plan hierarchy:** only Freelancer is navy and raised, with a larger price, a red button and a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \"Freelancers' pick\" stamp. Starter and Studio stay as quiet paper cards. On phones Freelancer now comes\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  first.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Copy for freelancers:** each plan has a \"for whom\" line (Testing the waters / Full-time freelancers /\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  You + a few collaborators). Freelancer carries a \"pay about 6 days faster\" claim and a \"about a coffee a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  week\" price anchor. Buttons and fine print are plan-specific.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Fixes from v1:** the double-border glitch is gone. The slider now puts a yellow \"Your pick\" tag on the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  card instead of the gold ring. The comparison table tints the Freelancer column.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Kept from v1:** the billing toggle with its savings lines, the slider, the table, the guarantee, the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  FAQ, the testimonial and the integration row.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Checks**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Contrast:** the colour pairs I computed all pass 4.5:1 in light and dark mode, including the red button\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  text and the small stamp-red text. The lowest is 4.75:1.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Phone overflow:** none at 360, 390 and 768 px wide.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Looked at:** the desktop and phone render of the top of the page. The logo spacing, the stamp collision\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and the headline wrap are fixed. Freelancer is clearly the card the eye lands on.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The \"Syncs with\" row is plain text, the 6-day figure is made up like the other content, and \"2 months free\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  is rounded (the real saving is 20%, about 2.4 months). I haven't opened the dark-mode render. `_renders/` is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  still in the working directory, and I'll delete it at the end as you asked. The first version is at\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `/tmp/pricing-v1/pricing.html`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ▪ Step 3/8 done\u001b[0m\r\n"]
