[611.909, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 5/8 · Range is done. I added the \"no surprises\" strip, the fixes for what the red team found, and one\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  regression catch of my own. All are in `pricing.html`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What changed**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **No-surprises strip** (the edge I took): four receipt-style lines under the plans. They say trials end on\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Starter and are never auto-billed, yearly plans have a 30-day refund, there is no fee markup, and every\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  payment gets a receipt. On phones the strip stacks into one column.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Trial fix:** the trial buttons now say \"No card · never auto-billed\", and the FAQ has a new \"What\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  happens when my free trial ends?\" answer.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Toggle note:** a line under the billing toggle changes with the period. Yearly shows \"billed up front,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  full refund within 30 days\". Monthly shows \"renew each month, cancel anytime\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Screen readers:** the table's \"—\" and \"✓\" now read as \"Not included\" and \"Included\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Footer:** it now says Inkwell is a fictional product made as a design exercise. You can remove that line\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  if you want the page to read as fully real.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What I caught on my own.** The new screen-reader text made the page 548 px wide on a 360 px phone, so it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  scrolled sideways. I fixed it by making the table container the positioning parent. I re-ran the overflow\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  check at 360, 390 and 430 px and it passes at all three, with no horizontal scroll.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What I looked at.** I looked at the desktop render and the phone render of the new strip. I did not re-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  render the dark mode view this round. The new strip uses the same colour variables as the rest of the page,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  but I haven't seen it in dark mode.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Where the page stands.** It shows the three plans, with Freelancer clearly the pick. It has a two-slider-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  plus-checkbox picker and the no-surprises strip. Its comparison table is accessible.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I took no new direction from the Stripe-style field, because that bar was already met in step 3. `_renders/`\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  is still in the working directory. It will be deleted at the end.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ▪ Step 5/8 done\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[613.978, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m⚑ Stop hook: Step 6 of pushing the work further: Judge. Open your first message with this line on its own,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m  exactly: `▸ Step 6/8 · Judge`. Write that line nowhere else.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ⎿  … +17 lines of instructions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[639.826, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 6/8 · Judge\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I'm building a check that isn't me, so I'm not grading my own work. It's a script that loads the page in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  real Chrome and measures it. It computes contrast from the rendered colours of every text element, checks\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  for sideways scrolling at six widths, and checks the price maths and that the cards and table agree. It also\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  checks the form labels and heading structure, and it measures whether Freelancer visually dominates. I'll\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  run the same contrast and overflow checks on v1 to compare.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
