[788.896, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 6/8 · Judge is done. The final page passes every check I ran, and it beats v1 on each one. The\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  5-second test, though, rests on measurements and my own look, not on a real person.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The outside check.** I wrote a script (`_renders/run.html`) that loads the page in real Chrome at six\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  widths and in forced dark mode. It measures:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Contrast of every text element, using its rendered colours.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Sideways scrolling.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The price maths.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Agreement between the plan cards and the comparison table.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The picker logic.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Form labels and heading structure.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Whether Freelancer visually dominates the other cards.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Results for the final page**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Check | v2 (final) | v1 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Lowest text contrast, light | 4.75:1 (161 elements) | 2.49:1, fails (the table's \"—\") |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Lowest text contrast, dark | 5.35:1 | 3.17:1, fails |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Sideways scroll (360 to 1280 px) | none at any width | none at 390 px |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Freelancer has the biggest price, the only distinct card colour, and is highest or first | yes | no |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Price maths, cards match table, picker logic | all pass | not applicable (no picker) |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Labelled inputs, one h1, no empty buttons | pass | pass |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Against the restatement**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Looks like a real, specific brand:** the invoice theme shows in the render. v1 reads as a generic\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  template.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Plan hierarchy and microcopy steer to Freelancer:** in the v1-against-v2 render, Freelancer is the only\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  navy card, with the biggest price, the red button and the stamp. On a phone it now comes first. v1 had it\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  third in the eye's path.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Billing toggle with a simple price change:** passes.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Phone and contrast:** both pass.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Light motion only:** passes, since only the button hover moves.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Cold read.** I read the whole page text as a visitor would and fixed two contradictions:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Starter said \"forever\" and also \"Free while you're getting started\". It now says \"Free for as long as you\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  like\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The FAQ said changes are \"prorated\", which was ambiguous next to the 30-day refund. It now says upgrades\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  are prorated and cancelling keeps access until the paid period ends.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I re-ran the checks after those edits and they still pass. Some phrases repeat, such as \"No card\", but each\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  sits where a visitor would be wondering about it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What isn't verified.** A real person hasn't done your 5-second test. The checks show Freelancer is the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  most prominent card by size, colour and position, and I looked at the render. That is a proxy, so please do\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the real test yourself in your final review. On a phone, the comparison table scrolls sideways, which is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  normal, but nothing hints at it.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `_renders/` still holds the test files and renders, and I'll delete it in the final step.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ▪ Step 6/8 done\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[789.718, "o", "\r\n\u001b[33m⚑ Stop hook: Step 7 of pushing the work further: Stretch. Open your first message with this line on its own,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[33m  exactly: `▸ Step 7/8 · Stretch`. Write that line nowhere else.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m  ⎿  … +15 lines of instructions\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[841.283, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 7/8 · Stretch\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **The stretch target.** So far the page tells visitors what they'll pay. The harder version shows them. A\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  freelancer's biggest question is \"what will I be charged, and when?\", and the best answer is the document\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the product itself produces, an invoice. The page will generate a live Inkwell invoice for the plan the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  picker recommends, in the billing period they've chosen. It will show the line items, the trial credit, \"Due\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  today: $0.00\", and the real calendar date the trial ends, worked out from today's date.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  This is harder than the earlier steps because the dates and totals have to be exactly right in every plan\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and period combination, including month and year rollovers and leap years. A wrong date on a page about\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  billing trust would do real damage. I also have to keep it consistent with the \"never auto-billed\" promise,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  so it can't say \"then we charge you\". It says \"keep it or drop to Starter\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Fallback:** the current page, which already passes every check. I'm saving a copy first, and I'll keep\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  that version if the stretch doesn't hold up. **Where it would likely break:** the date maths, the crowding\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  of the picker area, and a contradiction with the billing promises.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[841.931, "o", "\r\n\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 1 shell command\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(mkdir -p /tmp/pricing-pre-stretch && cp \"<workspace>/pricing.html\" /tmp/pricing-pre-stretch/pric…\u001b[0m\r\n"]
