[1019.501, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ▸ Step 7/8 · Stretch is done. The stretch held, so I kept it, and the fallback copy is at `/tmp/pricing-pre-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  stretch/pricing.html`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What I built.** Next to the \"Count your work\" picker there is now a live invoice, titled \"Your first\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  invoice\" and dated today.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Contents:** it shows the plan the picker recommends, in the billing period you've chosen. Line items\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  show the monthly rate times months, the 14-day trial credit, and \"Due today: $0.00\".\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Trial note:** it gives the real trial-end date, worked out from the visitor's clock. Today that reads\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  Dec 8, 2026.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Consistency:** the wording matches the \"never auto-billed\" promise. It says \"Keep Freelancer for $144.00\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  a year. If not, you drop to Starter at $0, with nothing to cancel.\" Starter shows $0.00 and \"we'll never ask\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  for a card.\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Layout:** the picker and the invoice sit side by side on desktop and stack on phones.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What the checks showed**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Invoice contents:** all five plan and period combinations are correct, with the right totals, trial\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  credit and wording.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Date maths:** Nov 24, 2026 gives Dec 8, 2026. Dec 25, 2026 gives Jan 8, 2027 (year rollover). Feb 20,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2028 gives Mar 5, 2028 (leap year).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Everything earlier still passes:** lowest contrast is 4.75:1 in light mode and 5.35:1 in dark, there's\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  no sideways scroll at any width, and the price maths, card/table agreement and picker all pass.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Rendered and looked at:** desktop, plus light and dark phone. The invoice reads as a real invoice.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Where it nearly broke**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - My test script first failed three times. Each failure was a bug in the test, not the page: a case-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  sensitive match, a capital \"Keep\", and a space my edit stripped. I corrected the test each time and did not\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  loosen the page's checks.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The invoice date comes from the visitor's computer clock. If someone's clock is wrong, the date on their\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  page is wrong, which is acceptable for a demo but not for a real billing page.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `_renders/` still holds the test harness and screenshots, and I'll delete it in the final step.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ▪ Step 7/8 done\u001b[0m\r\n"]
