[1066.231, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ ## Report\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **You asked for → it became**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - *A pricing page for a freelancer invoicing app, as a single web page* → one self-contained file,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `<workspace>/pricing.html` (30 KB, no external requests).\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - *A design showcase with believable content* → a fictional brand, Inkwell, built around one idea: the page\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  is an invoice. It has invoice-header metadata, perforated plan stubs, a \"Freelancers' pick\" stamp and a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  monospace/serif type pairing.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - *A look that is a specific brand, not a template* → cream, navy and stamp-red colours, plus a small\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  fictional-product line in the footer.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - *Plan hierarchy and microcopy that make the pick obvious* → Freelancer is the only navy, raised card, with\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the biggest price and a red button. Each plan has a \"for whom\" label. On phones Freelancer comes first.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - *Billing toggle with a simple price change* → kept, with savings lines and a note on how each period is\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  billed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - *Works on a phone, readable contrast* → no sideways scroll from 360 px to 1280 px, and light and dark mode\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  both pass.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Against the first version.** The final is better on every part of the ask, and I know of nothing it gave\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  up. It also adds a picker, an invoice preview, a \"no surprises\" strip, an accessible table and extra FAQ.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Check | v1 | Final |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  |---|---|---|\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Lowest text contrast, light | 2.49:1 (fails) | 4.75:1 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Lowest text contrast, dark | 3.17:1 (fails) | 5.35:1 |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Freelancer is the biggest price and the only distinct card | no | yes |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  | Plan shown first on a phone | Starter | Freelancer |\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Outside check.** A script loads the page in real Chrome at six widths, in light and forced dark mode. On\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the final page everything returned pass:\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Contrast over 160 text elements.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - No overflow.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Price maths.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Cards match the table.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - The picker's logic.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Invoice lines for five plan and period combinations.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Date arithmetic, including the year rollover and a leap year.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - Form labels and heading structure.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I also read the full page text as a visitor would and fixed two contradictions. The 5-second test has not\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  been done by a real person.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Stretch.** The target was a live invoice that shows exactly what a visitor would pay and the real trial-\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  end date, consistent with the \"never auto-billed\" promise. It worked. The only failures were three bugs in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  my own test, and I fixed those in the test, not the page.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Locked in.** You asked for nothing extra in the project, so I put nothing there. The check script is at\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `/tmp/pricing-check/run.html`, and it only lasts until `/tmp` is cleared. I created no CLAUDE.md note or\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  project command. To rerun it, copy `pricing.html` next to `run.html`, then run this and read the JSON in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `<pre id=\"out\">`. Use `w=360` for phones, and `sed 's/(prefers-color-scheme: dark)/all/'` to make a dark\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  copy.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \"/Applications/Google Chrome.app/Contents/MacOS/Google Chrome\" --headless=new --allow-file-access-from-files\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  --virtual-time-budget=5000 --dump-dom \"file:///tmp/pricing-check/run.html?page=pricing.html&w=1280\"\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  ```\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  The pre-step version is saved at `/tmp/pricing-pre-stretch/pricing.html`, and the very first version at\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  `/tmp/pricing-v1/pricing.html`.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Assumptions.** None: you answered every question, so I made no judgement calls on your behalf.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Open decisions**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  1. **Keep the check script?** I'd put `check-pricing.html` beside the page, with a three-line note in\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  CLAUDE.md.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - For: the check is repeatable and catches regressions.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - Against: you said you want nothing extra in the project.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - My pick: keep it in `/tmp` unless you plan to keep editing the page. Owner: you, before you next edit\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  the page.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  2. **Keep the \"fictional product\" footer line?**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - For: it prevents the made-up stats, testimonial and prices from being mistaken for claims.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - Against: it slightly weakens the \"could pass for a real page\" effect.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m     - My pick: keep it. Owner: you, at final review.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  3. **Run the real 5-second test.** Show the three cards to two or three people for five seconds each and ask\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  which plan they'd pick. Aim for Freelancer, and if it isn't, the hierarchy needs another pass. Owner: you,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  with the final review.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **Metrics**\u001b[0m\r\n"]
